---
import Layout from "../../../layouts/Layout.astro";
import DocsPreview from "../../../components/DocsPreview.astro";
import DocsSidebar from "../../../components/DocsSidebar.astro";
import DocsTOC from "../../../components/DocsTOC.astro";
import DocsPagination from "../../../components/DocsPagination.astro";
import CodeWindow from "../../../components/CodeWindow.astro";
import PropsTable from "../../../components/PropsTable.astro";
import "../../../styles/docs.css";
---

<Layout title="motion-marker — Motion Components" description="A highlighter stroke that sweeps behind a phrase when it scrolls into view. Follows text that wraps across lines." noMain>
  <div class="layout">
    <DocsSidebar />

    <main id="main">
      <h1><motion-split by="chars" interval="0.025" duration="0.5">motion-marker</motion-split></h1>
      <p class="lead">A highlighter stroke that sweeps behind a phrase when it scrolls into view, the way you would mark a printed page. It follows text that wraps across lines, and the text itself never changes.</p>

      <h2>Preview</h2>
      <DocsPreview replayId="marker-demo">
        <p class="sentence">Ship motion that feels <motion-marker id="marker-demo">physical, not mechanical</motion-marker>.</p>
      </DocsPreview>
      <h2>Import</h2>
      <CodeWindow
        filename="app.ts"
        copy
        code={`import 'motion-components/motion-marker'   // just this one
import 'motion-components'               // or the whole library`}
      />

      <h2>Usage</h2>
      <CodeWindow filename="index.html" copy code={`<p>Ship motion that feels <motion-marker>physical, not mechanical</motion-marker>.</p>`} />

      <h2>Color</h2>
      <p>Set <code>--mc-marker-color</code>. A transparent color keeps the text readable.</p>
      <DocsPreview replayId="marker-color">
        <p class="sentence">Every spring is <motion-marker id="marker-color" style="--mc-marker-color: rgb(96 165 250 / 0.35)">interruptible</motion-marker>.</p>
      </DocsPreview>
      <CodeWindow filename="index.html" copy code={`<motion-marker style="--mc-marker-color: rgb(96 165 250 / 0.35)">interruptible</motion-marker>`} />

      <h2>Text that wraps</h2>
      <p>On a phrase that wraps, every line gets its own stroke, and all of them draw together.</p>
      <DocsPreview replayId="marker-wrap">
        <p class="sentence narrow">Drop in a tag and <motion-marker id="marker-wrap">the spring comes free with every single component</motion-marker>.</p>
      </DocsPreview>

      <h2>In a sentence</h2>
      <p>Mix the marks and draw them one after another with <code>delay</code>.</p>
      <DocsPreview replayId="marks-sentence">
        <p class="sentence" id="marks-sentence">Replace the <motion-strike>manual checklist</motion-strike> with <motion-marker delay="0.5">one HTML tag</motion-marker>, <motion-underline delay="1">tested</motion-underline> and <motion-ring delay="1.5">reversible</motion-ring>.</p>
      </DocsPreview>
      <CodeWindow filename="index.html" copy code={`<p>
  Replace the <motion-strike>manual checklist</motion-strike>
  with <motion-marker delay="0.5">one HTML tag</motion-marker>,
  <motion-underline delay="1">tested</motion-underline>
  and <motion-ring delay="1.5">reversible</motion-ring>.
</p>`} />

      <h2>Properties</h2>
      <PropsTable nameLabel="Attribute" rows={[
        { name: 'trigger', type: 'string', default: "'view'", description: "What draws the mark: <code>'view'</code> when it scrolls into view, <code>'hover'</code> on pointer enter (it undraws on leave), or <code>'mount'</code> when it connects" },
        { name: 'duration', type: 'number', default: '0.6', description: 'Spring duration of the drawing, in seconds' },
        { name: 'delay', type: 'number', default: '0', description: 'Seconds to wait before drawing. Use it to draw several marks in one sentence one after another' },
        { name: 'bounce', type: 'number', default: '0', description: 'Spring bounciness. <code>0</code> keeps the stroke from overshooting the text' },
        { name: 'once', type: 'boolean', default: 'true', description: 'With <code>trigger="view"</code>, draw only the first time. Set <motion-code-inline copy>once="false"</motion-code-inline> to undraw when it leaves and draw again on every entry' },
        { name: 'threshold', type: 'number', default: '0.6', description: 'Share of the element, from 0 to 1, that must be visible before it draws' },
      ]} />

      <h2>CSS custom properties</h2>
      <PropsTable nameLabel="Property" rows={[
        { name: '--mc-marker-color', type: 'color', default: 'rgb(250 204 21 / 0.4)', description: 'Color of the highlighter stroke' },
      ]} />

      <h2>JavaScript API</h2>
      <p>The mark has the shared playback API: <code>play()</code> draws it, <code>cancel()</code> removes it, <code>finish()</code> shows it fully drawn and <code>replay()</code> draws it again from the start. It fires <code>motion-start</code>, <code>motion-finish</code> and <code>motion-cancel</code>. See the <a href="/docs/js-api/">JavaScript API</a>.</p>

      <h2>Accessibility</h2>
      <p>The mark is decoration: the text stays real, selectable and read by screen readers exactly as written. If the highlight carries meaning, wrap the component in <code>&lt;mark&gt;</code>. Respects <code>prefers-reduced-motion</code>: the mark appears fully drawn at once, with no animation.</p>
      <DocsPagination />
    </main>
    <DocsTOC />
  </div>
</Layout>

<script>
  import "motion-components/motion-marker";
  import "motion-components/motion-ring";
  import "motion-components/motion-split";
  import "motion-components/motion-strike";
  import "motion-components/motion-underline";
</script>

<style>
  .sentence {
    font-size: 1.6rem;
    font-weight: 700;
    letter-spacing: -0.02em;
    line-height: 1.5;
    color: var(--color-text);
    text-align: center;
  }
  .narrow {
    max-width: 18rem;
    margin-inline: auto;
  }
</style>
